gxR(){return"Does LastStats scrobble my music?"},
gxD(){return"No. LastStats is a visualisation app: it displays the scrobbles already recorded on your Last.fm account, but it does not record any itself.\n\nTo automatically scrobble your music, use a dedicated app such as Pano Scrobbler (available on Android)."},
gxW(){return"Is an iOS version planned?"},
gxI(){return"No. An iOS version is not planned at this time."},
gxX(){return"Does the app work on macOS or other platforms?"},
gxJ(){return"LastStats is developed and tested on Android. Behaviour on other platforms (macOS, Windows, Linux\u2026) is unverified, bugs or unexpected behaviour may occur."},
gxY(){return"Is LastStats open source?"},
gxK(){return"Yes! The source code is freely available on GitHub. The project is independent, built with passion by SanoBld. Feel free to contribute, report bugs, or leave a star \u2b50."},
gxZ(){return"Where is my data stored?"},
gxL(){return"On your device only. LastStats has no server: your scrobbles are cached locally for fast access, and your Last.fm credentials are stored locally too. Nothing is sent anywhere except Last.fm's official API."},
gy_(){return"How do I enable favorites?"},
gxM(){return"Go to Settings > Account and enter your Last.fm secret key. Once connected, you'll be able to favorite tracks directly from the app."},
gy0(){return"What is a 'scrobble'?"},
gxN(){return"A scrobble is a track logged as played on your Last.fm account \u2014 it's Last.fm's own term for 'one counted listen'. All your totals (top artists, stats, etc.) are based on it."},
gy3(){return"How do levels and achievements work?"},
gxO(){return"Your account level grows with your total scrobble count (there's no max level). Cards also get a border (bronze \u2192 iridescent) based on how many times that artist/track/album has been played. Everything is computed automatically from stats already cached locally, with no extra network calls."},
gy4(){return"How does power saving mode work?"},
gxP(){return"Power saving mode spaces out automatic syncs to save battery. It can be always on, follow your phone's own power saving mode, or turn on below a battery level you choose, from Settings > General."},
gxS(){return"How do I back up or restore my data?"},
gxE(){return"Go to Settings > Backup. You can export a backup file (with or without your Last.fm key) and re-import it later or on another device."},
gxT(){return"Does the app work offline?"},
gxF(){return"Yes, to some extent. Stats already loaded stay available offline thanks to local caching, but a connection is still needed to fetch new scrobbles."},
gxU(){return"Can I switch Last.fm accounts?"},
gxG(){return"Yes. From Settings > Account, sign out and sign back in with a different username. The local cache is automatically reset to avoid mixing data."},
gxV(){return"How do I set up notifications?"},
gxH(){return"From Settings > Notifications, you can enable sync-complete alerts, choose how often they appear, or turn them off entirely."},
